            %p algebraic:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+cobordism"} algebraic cobordism
          %h2#references References
          %p
            There are two notions of “algebraic cobordism”, not closely related, one due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Snaith77"} Snaith 77
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#LevineMorel01"} Levine-Morel 01
          %h3#SnaithConstructiom Snaith’s construction
          %ul
            %li#Snaith77
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Snaith"}> Victor Snaith
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Towards algebraic cobordism
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9904-1977-14281-X"} doi:10.1090/S0002-9904-1977-14281-X
            %li#Snaith79
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Snaith"}> Victor Snaith
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic Cobordism and K-theory
            %li#GepnerSnaith08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"}> David Gepner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Snaith"} Victor Snaith
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the motivic spectra representing algebraic cobordism and algebraic K-theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0712.2817"} arXiv:0712.2817
          %p
            The construction in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Snaith77"} Snaith 77
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Conner-Floyd+isomorphism"} Conner-Floyd isomorphism
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Snaith%27s+theorem"} Snaith's theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theory"} multiplicative cohomology theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X(b)^*(-)
            out of a pair consisting of a homotopy commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-monoid"} H-monoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and a class
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in \pi_n(X)
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi B
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = B S^1
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BU%28n%29"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U(1)
            of the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            is a generator of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi BS
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_2(BS^1)\cong\mathbb{Z}
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
